{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe bridge project mapping (`.bridge_state/projects.json` — mapped keys + `legacy_default`)\ncan hold syntactically-valid-but-nonexistent or bot-invisible Jira project keys. Ticket F adds\nSYNTACTIC write-time validation only (deliberately: a live call in the `set_project` write path\ncouples a local config write to Jira availability/auth, adds latency/flakiness, blocks legitimate\nbootstrapping/provisioning order, and is TOCTOU-insufficient anyway). Ticket D adds an at-pass-time\nEXISTENCE/visibility preflight inside the reconcile pass (the authoritative mutation guard).\n\nNeither gives an operator an on-demand, non-blocking way to ask \"are my mapped keys + legacy_default\nactually visible to the bot right now?\" outside a full reconcile pass. The projects.json corruption\nincident (bug 05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27) would have been caught immediately by such a diagnostic.\n\n## Scope (approved: additive diagnostic on the BRIDGE surface only)\n\nAdd an OPT-IN, credential-conditional, READ-ONLY, ADVISORY live mapped-key/legacy_default visibility\ncheck to the existing `rebar bridge fsck` verb, gated behind a new `--live-visibility` flag.\n\nHard constraints (separation of concerns — Jira stays an optional extra):\n1. Live check lives ONLY on the bridge surface. Do NOT add it to core `rebar doctor`\n   (`src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py`) — that command is store/tracker health and MUST stay Jira-free\n   (no reconciler / `[agents]` optional-extra import from core doctor).\n2. Do NOT introduce a `bridge doctor` verb (epic 2f79 deliberately declined it — reuse `bridge fsck`).\n3. Reuse D's mapped-project visibility helper — ONE shared helper answers \"are the mapped keys +\n   legacy_default visible to the bot?\". Do NOT hand-roll a second Jira existence check (that is the\n   duplicated-existence-check parity smell this epic has been eliminating). This is why G depends_on D.\n   The shared helper is `rebar_reconciler.access_check.check_mapped_project_visibility(repo_root, *,\n   probe=None, client_cls, env=None, query_project=None, projects_store_mod=None) ->\n   ProjectVisibilityResult(status, required, visible, missing, detail)` where status is one of\n   {ok, missing, transport_unavailable, skipped}.\n4. Credential-conditional graceful degradation: the NEW fsck-layer step performs its OWN\n   `JIRA_URL`/`JIRA_USER`/`JIRA_API_TOKEN` presence check FIRST (mirroring `run_access_check`'s\n   `missing_credentials` contract in `access_check.py`) and, when any is absent/incomplete AND no\n   `probe=` is injected, emits an advisory `skipped` verdict with `reason=\"missing_credentials\"`\n   WITHOUT calling the probe. Only when creds are present (or a `probe=` is injected for tests) does\n   the step call `check_mapped_project_visibility(probe=...)`. This is the fsck layer bridging the\n   helper's own `transport_unavailable`-on-absent-creds behavior into the operator-facing\n   \"skipped — no live credentials\" advisory. The step MUST skip cleanly, NOT fail.\n5. Read-only + advisory: no Jira writes; no bridge-state mutation; the new step reports drift but does\n   NOT change `bridge fsck`'s existing pass/fail exit contract.\n\n## Surfacing the verdict (data flow when `--live-visibility` IS passed)\n\nTo keep the pinned `bridge_fsck.schema.json` output contract UNCHANGED (its `required` set and the\n`test_bridge_fsck_schema_pins_new_required_fields_and_integrity_kinds` contract test both fix the\ntop-level JSON to exactly `{unknown_event_types, binding_drift, store_integrity}` under\n`additionalProperties: false`), the `--live-visibility` advisory is rendered as human-readable lines\nto STDERR (a separate stream) in BOTH text and `--output json` modes. It is NOT added as a new field\nto the stdout JSON findings object, so no schema or schema-contract-test change is required and the\ndefault (no-flag) stdout is byte-identical to today. The step's structured verdict dict is returned by\na directly-unit-testable helper (`audit_mapped_project_visibility(...)`) which main() renders to stderr.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar bridge fsck --live-visibility` gains a mapped-project live-visibility step that, WHEN live\n  creds are present, lists each mapped key + legacy_default and reports visible / NOT-visible-to-bot\n  by calling the shared helper `access_check.check_mapped_project_visibility`; the advisory is written\n  to stderr and does not alter the exit code.\n- [x] WHEN live creds (`JIRA_URL`/`JIRA_USER`/`JIRA_API_TOKEN`) are absent/incomplete AND no `probe=` is\n  injected, the fsck-layer step's own presence check emits an advisory verdict\n  `{\"status\":\"skipped\",\"reason\":\"missing_credentials\"}` WITHOUT calling the probe, and `bridge fsck`\n  behaves exactly as today (no crash, exit contract unchanged).\n- [x] The visibility logic is the SAME helper D uses (`check_mapped_project_visibility`, injected via the\n  `probe=` seam) — no duplicate existence check; verified by test.\n- [x] Core `rebar doctor` imports remain Jira-free (no new reconciler/`[agents]` import reachable from\n  `_commands/doctor.py`); verified by test.\n- [x] The default `rebar bridge fsck` (no `--live-visibility`) stdout JSON contract is unchanged (exactly\n  `unknown_event_types`, `binding_drift`, `store_integrity`); `bridge_fsck.schema.json` and its contract\n  test are untouched.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN always-on unit tests in `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck.py`, run with\n`python -m pytest tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck.py -q`:\n- (a) creds-present path with a `probe=` injected showing a mapped key invisible → the step's verdict is\n  `status=\"missing\"` and names the invisible key.\n- (b) creds-absent path (no probe, empty/partial `JIRA_*` env) → the step's own presence check returns\n  `status=\"skipped\"`, `reason=\"missing_credentials\"`, no probe call, no hard failure, exit contract\n  unchanged.\n- (c) all-visible `probe=` → `status=\"ok\"`.\n- (d) core-`rebar doctor`-stays-Jira-free assertion (no reconciler import reachable from\n  `_commands/doctor.py`).\nAlso `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; no real network calls in tests (patch the `probe=` seam).\n\n## Notes\n- Depends on D for the shared visibility helper (`access_check.check_mapped_project_visibility`).\n- Same workflow as A/B/D: fresh worktree off origin/main, review-plan → sign-review → claim, RED→GREEN\n  TDD, make lint/typecheck + targeted pytest, commit -s with rebar-ticket trailer, push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786825242491948001,"uuid":"36aa6625-6cff-46bc-8f3a-1bec22c1a7c7"}